  "indicatorHint": "{id, select, biodiversity{Habitat quality and connectivity of green patches (BKompV biotope values, InVEST habitat quality).} air{Population-weighted pollution index from traffic, industry and heating; vegetation removes part of it.} noise{Share of residents below the 55 dB(A) daytime limit for residential areas (TA Lärm).} housing{Housing capacity relative to local jobs, and how full it is.} economy{Jobs available for residents and the budget trend.} shopping{Retail within walking distance (Huff model, 700 m).} recreation{Green space within 300 m (WHO) and summer cooling.} commuting{Mean commute distance and car share (MiD 2017 mode shares).} climate{CO₂ balance of land use and traffic, plus urban heat.} budget{Municipal budget relative to the starting budget.} other{}}",
  "@indicatorHint": {"placeholders": {"id": {"type": "String"}}},
  "indicatorSimpleHint": "{id, select, biodiversity{Do plants and animals have good connected homes?} air{Can everyone breathe clean air?} noise{Are homes peaceful?} housing{Is there enough room for people?} economy{Can people find work and does the town earn enough?} shopping{Can people reach shops easily?} recreation{Can everyone enjoy nature nearby?} commuting{Can people get where they need to go easily?} climate{Does the town stay cool and protect the climate?} budget{Does the town have enough money?} other{How is the town doing?}}",
  "@indicatorSimpleHint": {"placeholders": {"id": {"type": "String"}}},

  "indicatorFormula": "{id, select, biodiversity{Biotope values (BKompV) times maturity, reduced by threats from roads, industry and buildings and by fragmentation, then scaled with a species-area curve.} air{Emissions from traffic, industry and buildings spread with an exp(-d/300 m) kernel, vegetation removes part, and the resident-weighted mean becomes the score.} noise{Every source loses 20 dB per distance decade and forest or buildings attenuate further; each resident scores (65 dB - L) / 10, clamped to 0-1.} housing{100 x min(1, capacity / (jobs / 0.52)) x (0.5 + 0.5 x occupancy); zero without housing.} economy{100 x (0.6 x min(1, jobs / workers) + 0.4 x budget trend), the trend taken from the budget change in the last month.} shopping{Huff model with lambda = 2 over shops within 700 m walking distance, averaged over the residents.} recreation{Resident-weighted 0.7 x green space within 300 m plus 0.3 x (1 - delta T / maximum urban heat).} commuting{100 x (0.5 x (1 - mean distance / 20 km) + 0.5 x (1 - car share)) from the gravity commute model.} climate{100 x (0.7 x (1 - CO₂ per person / 2.5 t) + 0.3 x (1 - mean delta T / maximum urban heat)).} budget{The municipal budget divided by the starting budget, clamped to 0-100.} other{}}",
  "@indicatorFormula": {"description": "One-line description of how an indicator score is computed", "placeholders": {"id": {"type": "String"}}},

